# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("`rebuild`": a generation is built at the end of the tick its dynamic changes, under a new `#g`, and the old one leaves at the end of that tick; "What a `rebuild` hands back": a plain result gives `$a`) and ch. 7 as ruled (round 3 ST: a `rebuild`'s result is structural, its update fires the tick after the generation is built, and that tick is owed).
test a_generation_of_clauses

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="go")
    1/#0/0: Ui.Label(text="none")
    2: Ui.Label(text="zero")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  added:
    1/#1/0: Ui.Label(text="some 1")
    1/#1/1: Ui.Label(text="second")
  torn down:
    1/#0/0: Ui.Label(text="none")

tick 2
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="n1")
